<table align='CENTER' cellpadding='2' border='1' cellspacing='2' background='http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif'><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=10&y=2002">This Month</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=9&y=2002">September-2002</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=8&y=2002">August-2002</A></TD></TR><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=7&y=2002">July-2002</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=6&y=2002">June-2002</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=5&y=2002">May-2002</A></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><CENTER><font size=+2>September, 2002</font><BR></center><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Halls of Testing</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Saturday - September 21st 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Thanks, Ninden, for another great raid :><BR>
We had a rough start, but eventually the raid took off.  We really got moving about 2 hours after start time.  We all did very well.  Everyone was following istructions quickly and without question. There seemed to be quite a bit of laughing (and probably some drinking) going on.  We even started playing with CH orders to get our clerics familiar with the idea.  I'm sure we'll be using it quite often in the near future.  A total of 10 hours went by before we gave the dragons a break hehe.<BR>
We decided to give <i>Dozekar the Cursed</i> a poke before we called it a day.  That's a mean leezard.  There was a little confusion over the timing of the CH chain which caused a slight speedbump in the healing process hehe.  This cut our Dozekar adventure a little short.  No worries though.  For many, it was the first time we'd gotten to see him. For several, it was the first time to ever get devoured by him hehe.  All good learning experiences.  I'm sure we'll all be a little more wary the next time we play with Doz.<BR>
Here are da phat lewtz:<BR>
