<TD>Gotenn</TD><TD>Leather Gloves</TD></TR>
</TABLE></font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>EQ Fashion!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Sunday - September 15th 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>It's a little known fact that high elven womens' helms were in fashion shortly after the Luclin models came out.  That's right, they were something to admire, indeed.  Don't take my word for it, here's Keymarad modeling a Thuradin brand helm back in-the-day.<BR>
<CENTER>
<A href="http://www.guild-legerdemain.com/memberfiles/user1/key1a.jpg" target="key1">
<img src="http://www.guild-legerdemain.com/memberfiles/user1/key1b.jpg" border=0></A>
</CENTER>
Nice huh?<BR>
Unfortunately, these helms became a thing of the past; a rumor, a myth.  As quickly as they came, they were gone =/  I assume that VI removed them because of the horrible load times that came with all the Luclin models.  When it came down to it, womens' fashion just wasn't that important and was cut out of the picture.<BR>
<BR>
Recently, we had a CT event.  During that event, Samanthea's Skyshrine hat looked a little different than it normally does.<BR>
<CENTER>
<A href="http://www.guild-legerdemain.com/memberfiles/user1/sam1a.jpg" target="sam1">
<img src="http://www.guild-legerdemain.com/memberfiles/user1/sam1b.jpg" border=0></A>
</CENTER>
What does this mean?  Are the old hats back?  Was this just a fluke bug interracting with the new UI and shrink or illusion?  Who knows. At least we know that the models are at least still in EQ somewhere hehe.<BR>
<BR>
